      "text": "This is a right triangle, so the Pythagorean Theorem can be applied. First, we will label the unknown side as BC. We will then use the Pythagorean Theorem to find the length of BC. \n\n$$a^2+b^2=c^2$$\n\n$$16^2+BC^2=37^2$$\n\n$$BC^2 = 37^2 - 16^2$$\n\n$$BC^2 = 1296$$\n\n$$BC = \\sqrt{1296}$$\n\n$$BC = 36$$\n\nSo the length of BC is $\\boxed{36}$ units.\nThe answer is: 36",
