      "text": "We need to find the value of $BC$.  \nTo do that, we must find the areas of triangles $ABC$ and $ABD$.  \nThe area of triangle $ABC$ can be found as $\\displaystyle S_{ABC} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height}$.  \nLet $x$ be the value of BC, and $y$ be the value of AB, then $\\displaystyle S_{ABC} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times x \\times 16 = 8x$.  \nThe area of triangle $ABD$ can be found as $\\displaystyle S_{ABD} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height}$.  \nLet $z$ be the value of AD, and $w$ be the value of BD, then $\\displaystyle S_{ABD} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times z \\times 19 = \\frac{19z}{2}$.  \n\nTherefore, $\\displaystyle \\frac{1}{2} \\times 16x + \\frac{1}{2} \\times 19z = \\frac{19z}{2} + 8x$  \n\n$8x + 19z - 19z = 19z - 16x$  \n\n$8x = 16x$  \n\n$8x = 8x$ subtending two vertical angles. [asy]\npair A, B, C, D, X;\nA=(0,0);\nB=(0,12);\nC=(-16,0);\nD=(-35,0);\ndraw(A--B--D--A);\ndraw(B--C);\ndraw((0,1.5)--(-1.5,1.5)--(-1.5,0));\nlabel(\"$37$\", (B+D)/2, NW);\nlabel(\"$19$\", (C+D)/2, S);\nlabel(\"$16$\", (A+C)/2, S);\nlabel(\"A\", A, SE);\nlabel(\"B\", B, NE);\nlabel(\"D\", D, SW);\nlabel(\"C\", C, S);\n[/asy] \n\nNow we can solve the equation.  \nMultiplying both sides of the equation by two, gives us $\\displaystyle 16x = 2 \\times 16x + 37 - 52$.  \nSolving for $\\displaystyle x$, we get $\\displaystyle x = \\boxed{41}$.",
